[38;5;252m[1m## The bug[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mc2CastRay[0m's [38;5;10mswitch[0m has no [38;5;10mdefault[0m arm and the function has no final [38;5;10mreturn[0m. The C, compiled at [38;5;10m-O0[0m, falls through to [38;5;10mleave; ret[0m with [38;5;10m%eax[0m never written — so for any [38;5;10mtypeB[0m outside [38;5;10m{0,1,2}[0m it returns the [3mcaller's[23m leftover [38;5;10m%eax[0m. The Rust had [38;5;10m_ => 0[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
A C enum parameter is passed as a plain [38;5;10mint[0m, so this is a reachable input, not a theoretical one. I made it deterministic with a naked trampoline that seeds [38;5;10m%eax[0m with [38;5;10m0x5A5A5A5A[0m before a tail [38;5;10mjmp[0m: the C returned the sentinel, the Rust returned [38;5;10m0[0m. Fixed by making the exported [38;5;10mc2CastRay[0m a naked shim mirroring the C's own dispatch:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1masm
[0m[38;5;10mcmp esi, 2      ; unsigned, so negatives fall through too — matches GCC's `ja`
ja  2f
jmp <c2CastRay_impl>
2: ret          ; %eax untouched
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
